# Project.md sync (Nove Work)

`Project.md` is the source of truth for chapter AI strategy: chapter-card outlines, pre-generate, refine, word-count rules, and chapter memory.

When you change any of the following, **update `Project.md` in the same change**:

- `generate_chapter` / `preview_generate_chapter` / `refine_chapter` / `save_chapter` / `preview_chapter_outline_brief` / `generate_chapter_cards` / `plan_next_chapters` / `regenerate_chapter_outline` / `generate_chapter_plots` / `regenerate_chapter_memory` / `set_chapter_memory` / `update_novel_canon` / `sync_canon_settings`
- Related helpers: `assemble_outline_gen_brief` / `root_linked_plots_and_knowledge` / `build_canon_context` / `root_generate_reference` / `chapter_context`
- Related prompts in `src-tauri/src/prompts.rs` (`generate_chapter_*`, `refine_chapter_*`, `repair_*`, `repair_canon_*`, `outline_gen_brief`, `gen_chapter_cards_*`, `plan_next_chapters_*`, `gen_chapter_plots_*`, `extract_chapter_memory_*`, canon format helpers)
- `chapter_constraints.rs`, chapter memory extract/store timing, or `WORD_COUNT_TOLERANCE`
- Workspace UI behavior for those flows (root generate cards, root canon binding, refine modes, memory panels)

## How to update

1. Edit the matching section (§0 concepts, §1 outlines especially **§1.0 / §1.0.1**, §2 generate / §2.2b canon, §3 refine, §4 length, §5 memory, §6 UI).
2. Adjust the checklists if steps or entry points change.
3. Do not leave `Project.md` describing removed passes (e.g. length-repair LLM, memory-on-generate).
4. If outline materials change (root plot/knowledge cards, canon retrieval), update §1.0.1 in the same PR — do not leave the table claiming “人物 only”.

UI copy still follows `i18n-sync.mdc`; this rule is for strategy/docs only.
